_reasoning_coverage","rationale":"Positive and negative reporting have distinct meaning-preservation demands; valid alternative placement of not is accepted.","existingBankMatches":[],"guideRelationship":"Familiar taught/practice content; the corresponding lesson guide teaches this procedure. No unseen capacity claimed."},"source":null}},{"itemId":"6d0b535f-55bc-5fbf-a8a8-2b3bbbf28b75","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-P09","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-P09","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-draft.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 10, 11; activities 11; programme T1.K3; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-draft.json#ENG7-U01-P09","hint":"Identify the person receiving the request and the requested action.","feedback":"She asked us to wait there uses asked + person + to + verb.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"Waited cannot fill the infinitive position."},{"key":"b","text":"The person follows asked directly; the infinitive marker belongs before wait."},{"key":"c","text":"Asked + person + to-infinitive reports the request."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"claim":"reported_positive_request","scenario":"Which sentence correctly reports “Please wait here,” using asked?","requiredInference":"Recognise the same request frame in a fresh sentence; do not count a response-format change as new coverage.","solution":"She asked us to wait there uses asked + person + to + verb.","nearest":["ENG7-U01-P07"],"disposition":"intentional_practice_variant","rationale":"Recognise the same request frame in a fresh sentence; do not count a response-format change as new coverage.","existingBankMatches":[],"guideRelationship":"Familiar taught/practice content; the corresponding lesson guide teaches this procedure. No unseen capacity claimed."},"source":null}},{"itemId":"f4238e50-22d6-5a62-ab69-be478eef7c40","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-P10","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1"