ding source DA-A","locale":"en","text":"For the school magazine, each student must show two looks made with the same main item. Nobody is asked to buy new clothes.\n\nArpi chooses a plain waistcoat. For the first look, she wears it with a white blouse and formal trousers. For the second, she wears it over a striped T-shirt with jeans.\n\nThe magazine prints both pictures side by side. Readers are asked to notice what changes and what stays the same, rather than vote for the most expensive outfit.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"ce0ec976-4fc5-5b09-a3a1-e8d40b9a6ee3","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DA-23","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DA-23","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-a.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 16, 20, 21; activities 18, 21, 22; programme T1.K2, T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-a.json#ENG7-U01-DA-23","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The profile places the childhood interest before 2011 graduation and the 2013 studio.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The profile places the childhood interest before 2011 graduation and the 2013 studio."},{"key":"b","text":"The childhood interest precedes both adult events."},{"key":"c","text":"The studio comes after the childhood interest and graduation."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Chronology or contrast from READ-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R01","ENG7-U01-R03","ENG7-U01-R07"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DA-24","ENG7-U01-MA-23"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Reconstruct a designer''s three-stage chronology from this supplied profile, not the familiar general history of clothes.","completeSolution":"The profile places the childhood interest before 2011 graduation and the 2013 studio.","guideRelationship":"G07 teaches the shared procedure; its worked example does not provide this complete stimulus-specific answer.","protectionJudgment":"Retain as an author-proposed protected parallel variant: the stated new stimulus must be interpreted. Keep complete prompts, keys, scripts and source families out of Practice/Chapter Review. This is not independent new reasoning, empirical equivalence or specialist qualification.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-DA-READ-B","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"d8a06249-883b-5a8f-819a-382bd19d41f7","title":"Reading source DA-B","locale":"en","text":"This short profile is based on the Fashion and Design Chamber of Armenia. Vahan Khachatryan grew up in Yerevan with paintings by his grandfather around him.\n\nHis interest in making clothes began in childhood. He later studied fashion in Florence and graduated in 2011. He founded his own design studio in 2013.\n\nThe profile connects his work with the art he grew up with and with cultures he encountered while travelling.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"9f40b4cd-a8d7-585f-a3e6-e95f8a76b8e1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DA-24","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DA-24","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-a.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 16, 20, 21; activities 18, 21, 22; programme T1.K2, T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-a.json#ENG7-U01-DA-24","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The profile connects his work with the family art around him as he grew up.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The chronology puts interest before the studio and does not identify it as the childhood influence."},{"key":"b","text":"The profile connects his work with the family art around him as he grew up."},{"key":"c","text":"No such rule is stated."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Supported cultural information from READ-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R07","ENG7-U01-R08","ENG7-U01-R09"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DA-23","ENG7-U01-MA-24"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Retrieve this profile''s family-art evidence instead of transferring the familiar Nikolyan cultural-tradition answer.","completeSolution":"The profile connects his work with the family art around him as he grew up.","guideRelationship":"G07 teaches the shared procedure; its worked example does not provide this complete stimulus-specific answer.","protectionJudgment":"Retain as an author-proposed protected parallel variant: the stated new stimulus must be interpreted. Keep complete prompts, keys, scripts and source families out of Practice/Chapter Review. This is not independent new reasoning, empirical equivalence or specialist qualification.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-DA-READ-B","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"d8a06249-883b-5a8f-819a-382bd19d41f7","title":"Reading source DA-B","locale":"en","text":"This short profile is based on the Fashion and Design Chamber of Armenia. Vahan Khachatryan grew up in Yerevan with paintings by his grandfather around him.\n\nHis interest in making clothes began in childhood. He later studied fashion in Florence and graduated in 2011. He founded his own design studio in 2013.\n\nThe profile connects his work with the art he grew up with and with cultures he encountered while travelling.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"c1c2b141-2b6b-5e96-aa1e-930979c25853","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DA-25","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DA-25","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-a.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-a.json#ENG7-U01-DA-25","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The missing-button problem is solved with a spare button and help.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The missing-button problem is solved with a spare button and help."},{"key":"b","text":"The speaker explicitly did not need to buy a new one."},{"key":"c","text":"The speaker wore the waistcoat after the repair."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Main message of AUDIO-A","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-L01","ENG7-U01-L03","ENG7-U01-L05","ENG7-U01-L07"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DA-26","ENG7-U01-MA-25"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Follow a problem and resolution through the message; a generic preference for comfort cannot choose its actual outcome.","completeSolution":"The missing-button problem is solved with a spare button and help.","guideRelationship":"G07 teaches the shared procedure; its worked example does not provide this complete stimulus-specific answer.","protectionJudgment":"Retain as an author-proposed protected parallel variant: the stated new stimulus must be interpreted. Keep complete prompts, keys, scripts and source families out of Practice/Chapter 